ve. |\n| 5/28 | **Wallet enforcement at dispatcher.** Hard-cap $100/mo t2r, soft-alert $80/mo, graceful-degrade on cap-hit + **interactive cap-override** (Q-K): \"wallet exhausted; approve $X overage for this turn?\" with logged rationale. Separate GBrain operational wallet ($30/mo start) tracked on its own line. Burn dashboards. | Smoke test: synthetic 1000-turn burn at $0.15/turn aborts at turn ~600 with clear message + override path. GBrain wallet logs separately. |\n| 5/29 | **Sprint S1 review.** Pull JSONL, derive observed per-turn cost, project monthly burn vs $100 cap, decide if Q1 needs revision per precedence rule. Draft S2 subplan at `plans/subplans/S2.md`. **Cadence-sync entry** (per Pass 1 B-9 + Â§12): `logs/cadence-sync/2026-05-29.md` with Sprint state + Brain Wave state + cross-cadence dependencies. | Burn rate documented in `logs/wallet-revisions.jsonl`. S2 plan drafted. Cadence-sync entry exists. |\n| 5/30-6/4 | **Week 3 â€” catch-up + S2 prep.** Slack for unknowns surfaced in weeks 1-2. If everything green, start S2 early. | Either S1 catch-up items resolved, or S2 has already begun. |\n\n**S1 success criterion:** Alpha runs end-to-end on gwl-server as v0 â€” OpenClaw + Bun + GBrain installed at known-good versions; t2r dispatcher live with top-tier models both halves; v0 starter skill bundle loads via AGENTS.md resolver; G-27 envelope captures into `gwl-corpus`; 5-flavor signal capture writing honestly; wallet enforcement + interactive override works. John can start using v0 for arbitrary daily work in week 3 (5/30+) â€” no fabricated task thresholds, real-use shapes the data.\n\n### Sprint S2 â€” Real-use accumulation (target 2026-06-05 through 2026-06-18, 2 weeks)\n\n| Theme | Tasks |\n|---|---|\n| Real-use surfaces | Whatever John actually reaches for during S2 â€” projects, research, drafting, finance, code, trip planning. No staged-task framing. Signal capture (task-agnostic JSONL) is the diagnostic for *which* surfaces v0 nailed vs fumbled. |