{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PpJL1e2UY7AA1EXPyvadXj","type":"tool_result","content":"367\t\n368\t## 12. Cadence synchronization\n369\t\n370\t**Status:** locked from Pass 1 B-9\n371\t\n372\tSprints (agent-layer) and Brain Waves (brain-side) run in parallel per Q7 walkthrough. Without a sync mechanism the parallelism becomes drift. The sync is cheap, doc-based, no meeting required.\n373\t\n374\t**Mechanism:** weekly entry in `logs/cadence-sync/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`. Four bullets:\n375\t\n376\t- **Sprint state:** S<n> day-X status; current task; blockers.\n377\t- **Brain Wave state:** Wave-<n> Phase-X status; current task; blockers.\n378\t- **Specialist track state:** which v0 specialists are active; which are queued; which (if any) are flagged for demotion at the next review. (Reads \"no specialists active yet\" until S2 week 2; first meaningful entry ~2026-06-11.)\n379\t- **Cross-cadence dependencies:** items either track needs from the other this week.\n380\t\n381\tFirst entry: 2026-05-29 (S1 review day). Cadence: weekly through S3 close. Post-S3 cadence reviewed at promote-to-v1 gate.\n382\t\n383\tProvides a single artifact future-John (or future-agents) can read to understand \"where were we\" without reconstructing from sprint logs and Wave gates separately.\n384\t\n385\t---\n386\t\n387\t## 13. Workstream Track Summary\n388\t\n389\t**Status:** added 2026-05-16 per `PLAN-Master-Plan-Update-Specialists-2026-05-16.md` Â§C.\n390\t\n391\tThe Â§4 day tables are sprint-first â€” they answer \"what am I doing on 5/22?\". This section is the orthogonal three-workstream view that answers \"where is each track right now?\". John named three parallel workstreams (build different **GWL brains**; build out the **GWL agent harness/structures**; build out **specialized agents**); this table makes them explicit alongside the sprint cadence.\n392\t\n393\t| Sprint | Workstream A â€” Brains | Workstream B â€” Harness / Structures | Workstream C â€” Specialists |\n394\t|---|---|---|---|\n395\t| **S1** (5/15 â€“ 6/4) | Corpus accumulating (Wave 7 closed; Phase C Step A authored, paused). | t2r dispatcher + GUI integration landed (commits `3dd6cce2`, `6250cf5a`, `6482d06d`). 9-project picker. Wallet enforcement live. AgentMatrix tile cleanup (`99c6ccbf`). | (none â€” alpha-v0 ships as the generalist baseline) |\n396\t| **S2** (6/5 â€“ 6/18) | Corpus continues to accumulate from alpha-v0 daily use; GBrain operational wallet audit; Phase C remains paused. | Per-workflow-type adoption matrix; signal-capture extension; sleep-loop first mutation (skill scoring); resume-on-switch (carryon ~6/8). | Ship 2 specialists: `finance-alpha` (default project `family-finances`) + `code-alpha` (default project `gwl-v0-build`). Author `PLAN-Specialists-v0-Pattern.md`. |\n397\t| **S3** (6/19 â€“ 7/2) | Brain Wave 8 resumes; Phase C Step A QLoRA training on the v0-enriched corpus. | v0 polish + missing-skill identification from signal data; promote-to-v1 gate evaluation. | Ship 2-4 more specialists driven by S2 matrix (candidate pool: `math-research-alpha`, `teaching-alpha`, `drafting-alpha`, `trip-planning-alpha` â€” pick at S3 start). Specialist demotion (human-in-loop). |\n398\t| Post-S3 (if v0 â†’ v1 promote) | Brain Wave 9 (cognitive cells); LoRA training continues. | v1 GUI integration (cognitive-cell config visibility). | Specialists inherit v1 brain automatically (same dispatcher path). |\n399\t\n400\tThe table is **read-only**: the day-by-day source of truth for each cell stays in Â§4 (sprints) and Â§5 (parallel workstreams). Â§13 collates so the three-track view is one glance.\n401\t\n402\t**The user's framing:** \"part of the work flow is to build different GWL brains, part is to build out the GWL Agent/harnesses/structures and part will be to build out Agents with specialized skill sets/areas of emphasis.\" This table is the explicit home for that framing.\n403\t\n404\t---\n405\t\n406\t## 14. This document as a living plan\n407\t\n408\t**Status:** master\n409\t\n410\tThis file is the v5 master. It does *not* freeze at master-promotion the way some plan documents do â€” it is provisional, the form is provisional, and the matter (execution) will teach us where the plan was wrong.\n411\t\n412\tWhat that means in practice:\n413\t\n414\t1. **Edits land in this file** during S1+ execution, not in a v5.1 sibling. Each significant edit gets a one-line entry in `logs/decisions/` so the why is preserved.\n415\t2. **No Pass 3.** Bounded-iteration discipline holds (Pass 1 + Pass 2 are the critique passes; further refinement happens through execution-time edits, not new critique passes).\n416\t3. **Emerging gaps go to `LIVING-GAPS.md`** (a sibling created when the first execution-time gap surfaces). Gaps that need plan-level changes get promoted from `LIVING-GAPS.md` into edits here. Gaps that resolve in-flight just live in `LIVING-GAPS.md` as a record.\n417\t4. **The companion `GAPS-2026-05-14.md` is frozen at master-promotion.** It is the v4â†’v5 reconciliation as of today. Execution-time gaps don't go there; they go to `LIVING-GAPS.md`.\n418\t5. **Sprint S1 starts 2026-05-15.** The first task is the `PERSONA-DESIGN-Alpha-v0.md` memo. The rest of the schedule in Â§4 is the working plan; deviation is fine if logged.\n419\t\n420\t---\n421\t\n422\t## 15. Pickup for the next Cowork session\n423\t\n424\tThe plan is ready to execute. The next Cowork session should:\n425\t\n426\t1. **Read this file end-to-end.** Bring deep-think + project-manager + expert-coder-Win11 + deep-research skills active.\n427\t2. **Start Sprint S1 day-1 (5/15)** per Â§4: author `PERSONA-DESIGN-Alpha-v0.md`, verify bootstrap propagation for `expert-coder-Win11`, mirror skills-master â†’ canonical.\n428\t3. **Use the Claude Code Bridge for any host operation.** Paste-prompts are no longer in scope; if the agent finds itself composing a \"please paste this in PowerShell\" message, climb out and use the bridge.\n429\t4. **Log progress** per the project-manager skill discipline â€” `pm log` for cheap session entries, `pm log --decision` for choices with downstream impact.\n430\t5. **At S1 day-15 (5/29)**, run the S1 review per Â§4 and write the first cadence-sync entry per Â§12.\n431\t\n432\tThe plan is provisional. Edit it as you learn. The execution is the point.\n433\t\n434\t---\n435\t\n436\t## 16. v2.1 MoE landed â€” 2026-05-23 (smart cheap/expensive routing, ahead of schedule)\n437\t\n438\t**Status:** SHIPPED + smoke-tested on alpha-v0 with both halves working end-to-end.\n439\t\n440\tÂ§3 of this plan reserved \"smart cheap/expensive routing\" for v1+ and the local-student-vs-frontier gating for v2. The MoE work landed today crosses both lines deliberately: it's still frontier-driven, but it routes BY taste's complexity/utility judgment, AND it brings the local Ollama (Qwen 2.5 7B GPTQ-Int4) on the RTX 4070 into the Trivial-tier slot. Driver was acute cost pain: the user reported \"I just can't use gwl agents right now with the price point that I am seeing.\"\n441\t\n442\t### What shipped\n443\t\n444\t- **`sandbox-lab-gui/brain/dispatcher/routing-matrix.mjs`** â€” tier ladder renamed `local/cheap/standard/gold` (was `trivial/standard/high/gold`). New 4-tier `REASONING_TIER_TO_MODEL`: localâ†’`ollama/qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M`, cheapâ†’`anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5`, standardâ†’`anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6`, goldâ†’`anthropic/claude-opus-4-7`. Legacy `TIER_TO_MODEL` kept as Proxy alias mapping oldâ†’new tier names. `selectTier` accepts both v2 and v3 taste output schemas.\n445\t- **`sandbox-lab-gui/brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`** â€” (a) parser normalization for v3 schema (singular `skill_hint` â†” plural `skill_hints[]`, new `tool_hints[]`); (b) new export `loadSkillBundle` that loads named skill bodies into a `<skills-loaded>` block; (c) `callReasoning` accepts optional `skillsBlock` parameter and prepends to reasoning system prompt; (d) `dispatchTurn` wires skill-pull-on-demand + full `routing.layer0/1/2` block into the envelope; (e) `buildEnvelope` bumped to `schema_version: 'g27-v3'`; (f) Qwen + Llama 3.1 added to `PRICE_PER_1M_USD`.\n446\t- **`skills-master/taste-v0/SKILL.md`** â€” schema v3: plural `skill_hints: string[]` + `tool_hints: string[]`. Dropped the v2.1-Integrated `context_load` nested object (out of scope; deferred to v2.2 Context-Intelligence).\n447\t- **`Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`** â€” 13 daily-use agents migrated to `routing_strategy: \"tier-scaled\"` (finance-alpha, code-alpha, librarian, all `pm-*`). 29 research/legacy agents locked to `routing_strategy: \"fixed\"` with explicit `reasoning_model` (closed the latent footgun where `sigma`, `prime-coder`, `dean`, lambda/phi/ccr, all `w-*`/`s-*`, alpha-lorentz, alpha-linear would have fallen through to tier-scaled after the rename).\n448\t- **`sandbox-lab-gui/agent-chat-v0.mjs`** â€” 3-line routing banner after each turn (`[taste: ... (decision-source)]`, `[tier: X â†’ reasoning: Y]`, `[skills: ...]`). New `/cost` slash command shows MTD spend vs cap, last 24h, last 10 turns avg+range, tier mix breakdown from the wallet ledger.\n449\t- **Tests** â€” `+27 new tests across 7 files` (T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6, T7). Suite: **525 tests, 523 pass, 1 fail (pre-existing `glci-runner.test.mjs`, unrelated), 1 skipped**.\n450\t\n451\t### Smoke verification (live, 2026-05-23 PM)\n452\t\n453\t| Smoke | Input | tier | reasoning model | skills loaded | total cost |\n454\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n455\t| 1 | \"hi\" (pre-fix) | standard | claude-sonnet-4-6 | â€” | $0.0036 |\n456\t| 2 | \"hi\" (post-fix) | **local** | **ollama/qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M** (FREE) | â€” | **$0.0013** |\n457\t| 3 | \"Write a Python median-stream-two-heaps function w/ type hints\" | **cheap** | **claude-haiku-4-5** | **expert-coder** | $0.0077 |\n458\t\n459\tThe bug between smokes 1 and 2: `selectTier` only checked `output_schema_version === 'v2'`, but the v3 schema bump made the new parser emit `'v3'` â€” so trivial turns were falling to the v1 effort_class default branch (`standard`) instead of the max-rule. Fixed; smoke 2 verified.\n460\t\n461\tSmoke 3 proves both halves of MoE responsibility (b) work: taste correctly classified the request and named `expert-coder`; the dispatcher loaded that SKILL.md body into the reasoning prompt; the envelope's `routing.layer2.skills_loaded` records the realized load.\n462\t\n463\t### Cost-relief math\n464\t\n465\t- Pre-v2.1 baseline (gemini-3.5-flash both halves at $1.50/$9 per Mtok): ~$0.005-0.010 per turn for daily traffic.\n466\t- Post-v2.1 with Haiku 4.5 cheap-tier ($1/$5 per Mtok): -25% to -35% on $/turn â€” landed Day 1 on 13 daily-use agents.\n467\t- With Tier 1 LOCAL live (Qwen 2.5 7B on the 4070, $0/$0): trivial turns drop to ~$0.001 (Haiku taste only; reasoning FREE). Combined projection: -50% to -65% aggregate $/day on the 13 migrated agents.\n468\t\n469\t### Relation to the v0/v1/v2 ladder\n470\t\n471\t- **v0 unchanged.** Alpha-v0 is still the v0 vehicle; the t2r-architecture-purity demonstration still holds. The taste-half is still frontier (Haiku), the reasoning-half is frontier *unless* tier=local pulls in the on-box Qwen.\n472\t- **v1 partially anticipated.** Smart cheap/expensive routing was the v1 marquee. v2.1 lands the routing without the cognitive-cell substrate, so it's \"v1-routing on v0-cells.\" Not a violation of the ladder â€” a fast-forward of the routing dimension.\n473\t- **v2 partially anticipated.** Local LLM serving turns was the v2 marquee. v2.1 uses Qwen 2.5 7B FOR the trivial reasoning slot, not as a LoRA-distilled student. That's an early Tier-1-only local without the gating function. The full v2 (gating + LoRA students per cell) remains future work.\n474\t\n475\t### Bootstrap path forward (v2.2 â†’ v2.3)\n476\t\n477\t- **v2.2 (proposed):** shadow-mode local router. Once ~5000 G-27 v3 envelopes accumulate from real alpha-v0 use, train a Qwen 2.5 7B LoRA to predict (taste_model_chosen, complexity, utility) from raw user input. Run alongside hosted Haiku as shadow; measure agreement. Goal: â‰¥95% over 7 days.\n478\t- **v2.3 (proposed):** flip the local router to authoritative; Haiku becomes 1% audit + fallback for low-confidence decisions.\n479\t\n480\tThis is the v0 LoRA pipeline (Phase C, Wave 7 Â§G-32) bootstrapped by the data v2.1's envelopes are now collecting. The G-27 v3 envelope's `routing` block is the load-bearing data shape that makes v2.2 trainable.\n481\t\n482\t### Companion documents\n483\t\n484\t- Design plan: `PLAN-Alpha-v2.1-MoE-Only-2026-05-23.md` (570 lines).\n485\t- Execution plan with parallel sprints + cost-relief priority: `EXEC-PLAN-Alpha-v2.1-MoE-2026-05-23.md` (580 lines).\n486\t- Session log of the wave-by-wave execution: `SESSION-LOG-2026-05-23-v2.1-MoE.md`.\n487\t- Sub-agent scratch outputs: `.critique-scratch/v2-1-exec-{deep-think,expert-coder}.md`, `.critique-scratch/v2-focused-{deep-think,deep-research}.md`.\n488\t\n489\t### What's not in v2.1 (deferred per \"just MoE, nothing else\" gate)\n490\t\n491\tThe user's verbatim instruction kept this tightly scoped. Twelve OUT items from gemini-authored v2.1-Integrated explicitly deferred â€” see `PLAN-Alpha-v2.1-MoE-Only-2026-05-23.md` Â§1.2 OUT list. Highlights of what was NOT in scope and IS future work:\n492\t- Context-Intelligence 5-profile context pruning (v2.2 candidate)\n493\t- Observation masking (v2.3+)\n494\t- Auto-retry on degraded output / under-route alarm watcher (v2.2)\n495\t- Cache-control breakpoint redesign (v2.2 if pruning lands)\n496\t- MTD-aware tier escalation (v2.2)\n497\t- Tool-hints runtime binding (gated on OpenClaw `--allowed-tools` runtime-mutability verification; verified that `openclaw` is installed but contract not probed)\n498\t- `gwl-t2r-brain/` sibling-tree sync (diverged plugin path; deferred standalone PR)\n499\t- Wallet pre-flight cost estimate that shrinks for local-tier turns (v2.1.1 nice-to-have)\n500\t\n501\t### Open follow-ups for the user (low-cost, low-risk)\n502\t\n503\t- Run `alpha-v0` interactively (`node sandbox-lab-gui/agent-chat-v0.mjs`) and watch the new banner.\n504\t- Use `/cost` after a few turns to see the tier-mix breakdown.\n505\t- Add `ollama pull qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M` to `Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1` so future clones get Tier 1 LOCAL ready.\n506\t\n507\t---\n508\t\n509\t*End of Master Rollout Plan v5. Synthesized 2026-05-14. Pass 1 + Pass 2 critique embedded. Sprint S1 starts 2026-05-15. Edits landed: 2026-05-16 (specialists + carryon + tile cleanup + new Â§13 Workstream Track Summary per `PLAN-Master-Plan-Update-Specialists-2026-05-16.md`; Â§3/Â§4/Â§10/Â§12 amendments; existing Â§13/Â§14 renumbered to Â§14/Â§15); 2026-05-23 (Â§16 v2.1 MoE landed â€” smart cheap/expensive routing, local Qwen 2.5 7B as Tier 1, skill-pull-on-demand, +27 tests, 3 smokes green, -50-65% projected cost relief). v0 vehicle shipped as alpha-v0 in commits `6250cf5a`+`6482d06d` 2026-05-15/16; v2.1 MoE this commit.*\n510\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fccaeea6-5be8-4dd3-a02c-251164b5bb08","uuid":"6b74f27b-b531-4fad-bb87-6e5222252cae","timestamp":"2026-06-14T02:27:54.812Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\MASTER-PLAN-v5.md","content":"\n## 12. Cadence synchronization\n\n**Status:** locked from Pass 1 B-9\n\nSprints (agent-layer) and Brain Waves (brain-side) run in parallel per Q7 walkthrough. Without a sync mechanism the parallelism becomes drift. The sync is cheap, doc-based, no meeting required.\n\n**Mechanism:** weekly entry in `logs/cadence-sync/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`. Four bullets:\n\n- **Sprint state:** S<n> day-X status; current task; blockers.\n- **Brain Wave state:** Wave-<n> Phase-X status; current task; blockers.\n- **Specialist track state:** which v0 specialists are active; which are queued; which (if any) are flagged for demotion at the next review. (Reads \"no specialists active yet\" until S2 week 2; first meaningful entry ~2026-06-11.)\n- **Cross-cadence dependencies:** items either track needs from the other this week.\n\nFirst entry: 2026-05-29 (S1 review day). Cadence: weekly through S3 close. Post-S3 cadence reviewed at promote-to-v1 gate.\n\nProvides a single artifact future-John (or future-agents) can read to understand \"where were we\" without reconstructing from sprint logs and Wave gates separately.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Workstream Track Summary\n\n**Status:** added 2026-05-16 per `PLAN-Master-Plan-Update-Specialists-2026-05-16.md` Â§C.\n\nThe Â§4 day tables are sprint-first â€” they answer \"what am I doing on 5/22?\". This section is the orthogonal three-workstream view that answers \"where is each track right now?\". John named three parallel workstreams (build different **GWL brains**; build out the **GWL agent harness/structures**; build out **specialized agents**); this table makes them explicit alongside the sprint cadence.\n\n| Sprint | Workstream A â€” Brains | Workstream B â€” Harness / Structures | Workstream C â€” Specialists |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **S1** (5/15 â€“ 6/4) | Corpus accumulating (Wave 7 closed; Phase C Step A authored, paused). | t2r dispatcher + GUI integration landed (commits `3dd6cce2`, `6250cf5a`, `6482d06d`). 9-project picker. Wallet enforcement live. AgentMatrix tile cleanup (`99c6ccbf`). | (none â€” alpha-v0 ships as the generalist baseline) |\n| **S2** (6/5 â€“ 6/18) | Corpus continues to accumulate from alpha-v0 daily use; GBrain operational wallet audit; Phase C remains paused. | Per-workflow-type adoption matrix; signal-capture extension; sleep-loop first mutation (skill scoring); resume-on-switch (carryon ~6/8). | Ship 2 specialists: `finance-alpha` (default project `family-finances`) + `code-alpha` (default project `gwl-v0-build`). Author `PLAN-Specialists-v0-Pattern.md`. |\n| **S3** (6/19 â€“ 7/2) | Brain Wave 8 resumes; Phase C Step A QLoRA training on the v0-enriched corpus. | v0 polish + missing-skill identification from signal data; promote-to-v1 gate evaluation. | Ship 2-4 more specialists driven by S2 matrix (candidate pool: `math-research-alpha`, `teaching-alpha`, `drafting-alpha`, `trip-planning-alpha` â€” pick at S3 start). Specialist demotion (human-in-loop). |\n| Post-S3 (if v0 â†’ v1 promote) | Brain Wave 9 (cognitive cells); LoRA training continues. | v1 GUI integration (cognitive-cell config visibility). | Specialists inherit v1 brain automatically (same dispatcher path). |\n\nThe table is **read-only**: the day-by-day source of truth for each cell stays in Â§4 (sprints) and Â§5 (parallel workstreams). Â§13 collates so the three-track view is one glance.\n\n**The user's framing:** \"part of the work flow is to build different GWL brains, part is to build out the GWL Agent/harnesses/structures and part will be to build out Agents with specialized skill sets/areas of emphasis.\" This table is the explicit home for that framing.\n\n---\n\n## 14. This document as a living plan\n\n**Status:** master\n\nThis file is the v5 master. It does *not* freeze at master-promotion the way some plan documents do â€” it is provisional, the form is provisional, and the matter (execution) will teach us where the plan was wrong.\n\nWhat that means in practice:\n\n1. **Edits land in this file** during S1+ execution, not in a v5.1 sibling. Each significant edit gets a one-line entry in `logs/decisions/` so the why is preserved.\n2. **No Pass 3.** Bounded-iteration discipline holds (Pass 1 + Pass 2 are the critique passes; further refinement happens through execution-time edits, not new critique passes).\n3. **Emerging gaps go to `LIVING-GAPS.md`** (a sibling created when the first execution-time gap surfaces). Gaps that need plan-level changes get promoted from `LIVING-GAPS.md` into edits here. Gaps that resolve in-flight just live in `LIVING-GAPS.md` as a record.\n4. **The companion `GAPS-2026-05-14.md` is frozen at master-promotion.** It is the v4â†’v5 reconciliation as of today. Execution-time gaps do