e: **525 tests, 523 pass, 1 fail (pre-existing `glci-runner.test.mjs`, unrelated), 1 skipped**.\n\n### Smoke verification (live, 2026-05-23 PM)\n\n| Smoke | Input | tier | reasoning model | skills loaded | total cost |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"hi\" (pre-fix) | standard | claude-sonnet-4-6 | â€” | $0.0036 |\n| 2 | \"hi\" (post-fix) | **local** | **ollama/qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M** (FREE) | â€” | **$0.0013** |\n| 3 | \"Write a Python median-stream-two-heaps function w/ type hints\" | **cheap** | **claude-haiku-4-5** | **expert-coder** | $0.0077 |\n\nThe bug between smokes 1 and 2: `selectTier` only checked `output_schema_version === 'v2'`, but the v3 schema bump made the new parser emit `'v3'` â€” so trivial turns were falling to the v1 effort_class default branch (`standard`) instead of the max-rule. Fixed; smoke 2 verified.\n\nSmoke 3 proves both halves of MoE responsibility (b) work: taste correctly classified the request and named `expert-coder`; the dispatcher loaded that SKILL.md body into the reasoning prompt; the envelope's `routing.layer2.skills_loaded` records the realized load.\n\n### Cost-relief math\n\n- Pre-v2.1 baseline (gemini-3.5-flash both halves at $1.50/$9 per Mtok): ~$0.005-0.010 per turn for daily traffic.\n- Post-v2.1 with Haiku 4.5 cheap-tier ($1/$5 per Mtok): -25% to -35% on $/turn â€” landed Day 1 on 13 daily-use agents.\n- With Tier 1 LOCAL live (Qwen 2.5 7B on the 4070, $0/$0): trivial turns drop to ~$0.001 (Haiku taste only; reasoning FREE). Combined projection: -50% to -65% aggregate $/day on the 13 migrated agents.\n\n### Relation to the v0/v1/v2 ladder\n\n- **v0 unchanged.** Alpha-v0 is still the v0 vehicle; the t2r-architecture-purity demonstration still holds. The taste-half is still frontier (Haiku), the reasoning-half is frontier *unless* tier=local pulls in the on-box Qwen.\n- **v1 partially anticipated.** Smart cheap/expensive routing was the v1 marquee. v2.1 lands the routing without the cognitive-cell substrate, so it's \"v1-routing on v0-cells.\" Not a violation of the ladder â€” a fast-forward of the routing dimension.\n- **v2 partially anticipated.** Local LLM serving turns was the v2 marquee. v2.1 uses Qwen 2.5 7B FOR the trivial reasoning slot, not as a LoRA-distilled student. That's an early Tier-1-only local without the gating function. The full v2 (gating + LoRA students per cell) remains future work.\n\n### Bootstrap path forward (v2.2 â†’ v2.3)\n\n- **v2.2 (proposed):** shadow-mode local router. Once ~5000 G-27 v3 envelopes accumulate from real alpha-v0 use, train a Qwen 2.5 7B LoRA to predict (taste_model_chosen, complexity, utility) from raw user input. Run alongside hosted Haiku as shadow; measure agreement. Goal: â‰¥95% over 7 days.\n- **v2.3 (proposed):** flip the local router to authoritative; Haiku becomes 1% audit + fallback for low-confidence decisions.\n\nThis is the v0 LoRA pipeline (Phase C, Wave 7 Â§G-32) bootstrapped by the data v2.1's envelopes are now collecting. The G-27 v3 envelope's `routing` block is the load-bearing data shape that makes v2.2 trainable.\n\n### Companion documents\n\n- Design plan: `PLAN-Alpha-v2.1-MoE-Only-2026-05-23.md` (570 lines).\n- Execution plan with parallel sprints + cost-relief priority: `EXEC-PLAN-Alpha-v2.1-MoE-2026-05-23.md` (580 lines).\n- Session log of the wave-by-wave execution: `SESSION-LOG-2026-05-23-v2.1-MoE.md`.\n- Sub-agent scratch outputs: `.critique-scratch/v2-1-exec-{deep-think,expert-coder}.md`, `.critique-scratch/v2-focused-{deep-think,deep-research}.md`.\n\n### What's not in v2.1 (deferred per \"just MoE, nothing else\" gate)\n\nThe user's verbatim instruction kept this tightly scoped. Twelve OUT items from gemini-authored v2.1-Integrated explicitly deferred â€” see `PLAN-Alpha-v2.1-MoE-Only-2026-05-23.md` Â§1.2 OUT list. Highlights of what was NOT in scope and IS future work:\n- Context-Intelligence 5-profile context pruning (v2.2 candidate)\n- Observation masking (v2.3+)\n- Auto-retry on degraded output / under-route alarm watcher (v2.2)\n- Cache-control breakpoint redesign (v2.2 if pruning lands)\n- MTD-aware tier escalation (v2.2)\n- Tool-hints runtime binding (gated on OpenClaw `--allowed-tools` runtime-mutability verification; verified that `openclaw` is installed but contract not probed)\n- `gwl-t2r-brain/` sibling-tree sync (diverged plugin path; deferred standalone PR)\n- Wallet pre-flight cost estimate that shrinks for local-tier turns (v2.1.1 nice-to-have)\n\n### Open follow-ups for the user (low-cost, low-risk)\n\n- Run `alpha-v0` interactively (`node sandbox-lab-gui/agent-chat-v0.mjs`) and watch the new banner.\n- Use `/cost` after a few turns to see the tier-mix breakdown.\n- Add `ollama pull qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M` to `Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1` so future clones get Tier 1 LOCAL ready.\n\n---\n\n*End of Master Rollout Plan v5. Synthesized 2026-05-14. Pass 1 + Pass 2 critique embedded. Sprint S1 starts 2026-05-15. Edits landed: 2026-05-16 (specialists + carryon + tile cleanup + new Â§13 Workstream Track Summary per `PLAN-Master-Plan-Update-Specialists-2026-05-16.md`; Â§3/Â§4/Â§10/Â§12 amendments; existing Â§13/Â§14 renumbered to Â§14/Â§15); 2026-05-23 (Â§16 v2.1 MoE landed â€” smart cheap/expensive routing, local Qwen 2.5 7B as Tier 1, skill-pull-on-demand, +27 tests, 3 smokes green, -50-65% projected cost relief). v0 vehicle shipped as alpha-v0 in commits `6250cf5a`+`6482d06d` 2026-05-15/16; v2.1 MoE this commit.*\n","numLines":144,"startLine":367,"totalLines":510}}}
