{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UmdNCy1GuYTTMhG5h9uk3E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Master Rollout Plan v5 â€” Agent-First and the v0â€“v1â€“v2 Ladder\n\nGrounded summary of the planning session (single member doc: `MASTER-PLAN-v5.md`, dated 2026-05-14, MASTER/living; synthesized from two parallel Cowork v5 drafts; supersedes v4; two bounded critique passes, no Pass 3).\n\n## Core reframe (Â§1)\n- **v4 was brain-first; v5 is agent-first.** The deepest cut: **brain â‰  agent** â€” v4 fused them, v5 pries them apart (an agent is the persistent unit that *uses* a brain, with its own memory/skills/tools/planning loop).\n- **The agent layer is commoditized; the GWL t2r brain is the moat.** Strategy: assemble best-in-class commodity agent layer under a GWL brain, instrument the seam with quality-signal hooks, use it daily while the brain deepens underneath.\n- v5 originally planned to **borrow Garry Tan's GBrain wholesale** (MIT, OpenClaw-native) for ~80% of v0 agent-layer scope; GBrain's gap is the **quality-signal capture loop** (no skill scoring, Wilson-CI tournaments, RLHF/DPO, 5-flavor signals) â€” that gap is v5's marquee addition.\n\n## The v0/v1/v2 ladder (Â§3) â€” this is the agent-maturity ladder, **orthogonal** to the system version (`v2.1`)\n- **v0** = OpenClaw + GBrain + t2r dispatcher; goal is **Cowork-comparable daily use**. Both t2r halves are **top-tier frontier** (default Gemini Pro both, Opus per-turn escalation). No cognitive cells, no local LLMs. Wallet **$100/mo per agent** (soft $80, hard cap at dispatcher). Vehicle = **`alpha-v0`** (shipped 2026-05-16, commits `6250cf5a`+`6482d06d`).\n- **v1** = t2r with **cognitive cells** (frontier-driven, MoE-style routing inside each half); no LoRA yet.\n- **v2** = v1 cells **+ local QLoRA-trained 8B students per cell** on the 4070 + a **gating function** (local vs frontier per turn); wallet target **$300â€“700/mo** as ~40â€“60% of turns divert to local.\n- **Promotion gate** is a **per-workflow-type adoption matrix** (code/research/drafting/finance/trip-planning/PM tracked separately) â€” promote when **â‰¥3 types show â‰¥50% v0 adoption** with stable signal quality. No staged trust-ladder.\n- **GBrain operational wallet is separate** ($30/mo start) from the t2r wallet â€” a cap-hit there â‰  v0 failure.\n\n## The v0 build plan (Â§4) â€” dated, decomposed\n- **Sprint S1** (5/15â€“6/4, 3 weeks, week 3 = slack): persona-design memo â†’ `expert-coder-Win11`/PM propagation â†’ **B-11 namespace rename** (`gbrain/`â†’`gwl-runtime/`, `~/gbrain`â†’`gwl-corpus`, leave hole for Tan's GBrain; test gate must stay 498/498) â†’ Bun install (GBrain-only scope) â†’ OpenClaw+GBrain install â†’ `AGENTS.md` bridge â†’ **t2r dispatcher + routing.json per-half model fields** â†’ starter skill bundle â†’ Alpha conversion â†’ 5-flavor signal capture â†’ wallet enforcement with interactive cap-override â†’ S1 review.\n- **Sprint S2** (6/5â€“6/18): real-use accumulation; build the adoption matrix; ship **2 specialists** (`finance-alpha`, `code-alpha`); first sleep mutation (skill scoring, **human-in-loop, no auto-retire**); GBrain wallet audit; resume-on-switch (carryon).\n- **Sprint S3** (6/19â€“7/2): v0 polish + missing-skill ID; **2â€“4 more specialists** chosen from S2 data; **Brain Wave 8 / Phase C QLoRA** resumes on the 4070; promote-to-v1 gate evaluation.\n\n## Hooks meta-architecture (Â§6)\n- ~9 load-bearing hooks (`session_start`, `pre_turn`, `pre_tool_call`, `post_tool_call`, `post_turn`, `on_user_feedback`, `on_error`, `session_end`, `sleep_*`); GWL's contribution is **what gets written to JSONL** at each.\n- **Load-bearing insight: hooks themselves are learnable** (e.g. the `pre_turn` reuse-similarity threshold is a number sleep tunes) â€” cheapest learning in the stack, gross-margin-positive on day one.\n\n## Risk/contingency framing (Â§8, Â§11)\n- Top risks: GBrain harder-than-30-min install (mitigation: sacrificial spike + **vendored snapshot**); B-11 rename breaking the 498-test gate; **t2r ~2Ã— latency killing adoption** (a measured risk, not tunable â€” Q2 commits to top-tier-both).\n- **Three pre-named failure branches** if the S3 matrix is red: (a) proceed to v1; (b) targeted patch on failing workflow types; (c) \"rethink experiment\" â€” three candidates: drop the t2r split for single-call, try Opus both halves, or try Cowork+GBrain instead of OpenClaw+GBrain.\n\n## Two later edits embedded in the living doc\n- **2026-05-16 (Â§13):** added the orthogonal **three-workstream view** (Brains / Harness-Structures / Specialists) plus specialists + carryon.\n- **2026-05-23 (Â§16): v2.1 MoE SHIPPED ahead of schedule** â€” tier ladder `local/cheap/standard/gold` (localâ†’Qwen 2.5 7B on the 4070 = free, cheapâ†’Haiku, standardâ†’Sonnet, goldâ†’Opus); skill-pull-on-demand; `g27-v3` envelope; **+27 tests (523/525 pass)**; 3 live smokes green; **projected âˆ’50% to âˆ’65% $/day** on 13 daily-use agents. Framed as \"v1-routing on v0-cells\" â€” a fast-forward of the routing dimension, not a ladder violation.\n\n## Caveat on currency\nThis plan is **superseded for the agent-layer \"borrow GBrain wholesale\" strategy** by the 2026-05-27 in-doc update (Â§ \"Update â€” 2026-05-27\") and the later **Sovereign t2r Harness** convergence: GBrain was **demoted from \"the agent layer\" to a deferred offline training flywheel**, and the team built its own harness instead. Per repo memory, the current live state (2026-06) is the Crucible-forged harness-completion plan, well past this v5 snapshot â€” treat Â§1â€“Â§16 as the agent-first *origin* design, not current truth."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7400,"cache_read_input_tokens":73077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7400},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"d